/* The Missing Bees – MiniMystery Education (nature, ages 6–12). Texts and nature stations (EN).
   The beehive behind the school is empty: Miss Noor's bees have left. Bees only stay where there are enough flowers, water and
   hiding places. At nature stations around (or inside) the school, teams explore the neighbourhood with real observations: counting,
   looking, listening, feeling. Each station gives a nature key: a link in the cycle of nature. In the finale they put the cycle in
   order (sun → plant → animal → soil → plant): then they know what the bees need, and the bees come back.
   Levels: 0 = ages 6–8 (looking and counting, more/less, two pictures as answers, everything read aloud) · 1 = ages 8–10 (recognising
   species, food chain, seasons, measuring) · 2 = ages 10–12 (ecosystem, cycle, biodiversity, percentages, cause and effect).
   Per station: intro, act {out,in}, lvl[3] (kind text/choice/count), tip. Indoors: observations at the window, plants in the classroom,
   the school garden or the playground. */
